there is no let-up in this latest phase  of violence  the Gaza Strip battered by Israeli  airstrikes retaliation for the huge  barrage of rocket fire that has been  loosed on civilians across southern  Israel in major city as the sound of  sirens is a constant refrain as we  filmed at a house that had been hit by a  rocket ended up running for cover  sirens could just sound again we're in  Ashkelon without five kilowatts into the  Gaza Strip in here now the Iron Dome is  shooting rockets out of the sky but this  has been going on like this all day the  rockets and mortars that Hamas and other  Palestinian groups are firing are not  always intercepted this strike killed a  58 year old man in the early hours  peppering the building with shrapnel  Palestinians have also been burying  their dead this the funeral of a  pregnant woman and her infant niece but  Israel has denied it was responsible  saying they were killed by accidental  militant fire  Israel claims it strikes are only  hitting military targets but the owner  of this building cannot understand why  it was leveled by an Israeli bomb  I'm really surprised all the people who  are renting a businessman with business  offices and the residents who live here  are very poor they hardly pay any rent  every month had begged them to pay the  rent  I'm surprised and there is no reason at  all to target the building the IDF has  also carried out targeted strikes on  Hamas operatives this car was being  driven by a man Israel claims was  responsible for funneling Iranian money  to armed factions in Gaza sources within  the Israeli security establishment blame  into Palestinian factional rivalry for  the flare-up it seems as if the  Palestinian Islamic Jihad are trying to  drag everybody  Hamas themselves the Gaza Strip and  Israel into some kind of escalation  we have signaled very clearly to Hamas  that we hold them responsible for every  act of violence that comes from the Gaza  Strip towards Israel and we will  retaliate against them Hamas no claims  it is Israel's failure to deliver on  conditions of the previous ceasefire  that have led to the breakdown it is  hard to read where this goes next but  with Israel due to host the Eurovision  Song Contest in the next 10 days the  stakes could not be higher the Egyptians  and the United Nations are trying to  broker another ceasefire to end this  round of violence  but for now the fighting goes on and the  suffering on both sides continues Alex  Rossy Sky News Ashkelon in southern  Israel
 

